---
import PlayingCard from '../components/PlayingCard.svelte';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'goal', title: 'The goal' },
  { id: 'deal', title: 'The deal & the crib' },
  { id: 'passing', title: 'Passing' },
  { id: 'play', title: 'Playing a hand' },
  { id: 'scoring', title: 'Scoring' },
  { id: 'shooting', title: 'Shooting the Moon & Sun' },
  { id: 'ending', title: 'Ending the game' },
  { id: 'online', title: 'Playing online' },
];
---

<Layout title="How to play" description="How to play Hearts with our house rules: Jack of Diamonds, the crib, Shooting the Sun and more.">
  <div class="container page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="stack" style="--gap: 8px">
        <span class="eyebrow">How to play</span>
        <h1 class="display">Hearts, house rules</h1>
        <p class="muted lede">
          Classic Hearts with a few family twists: a −10 Jack, a secret crib, and the rare, glorious Shooting the Sun.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="layout">
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        {sections.map((s) => <a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a>)}
      </nav>

      <article class="stack doc" style="--gap: 20px">
        <section id="goal" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>The goal</h2>
          <p>
            Hearts is a trick-taking game where points are bad. Every heart you take costs you, the Queen of Spades costs you a
            lot, and the Jack of Diamonds helps you. The <strong>lowest score wins</strong>. Our game runs over many hands, often
            the whole year, so the running total is what matters.
          </p>
          <p>
            It’s played with <strong>4 or 5 players</strong> and a standard 52-card deck (minus three twos with five players).
            Aces are high.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="deal" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>The deal & the crib</h2>
          <p>
            Before anyone sees their cards, a few are set aside face down in the middle. That’s the <strong>crib</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <div class="crib-demo" aria-hidden="true">
              <PlayingCard width={56} />
              <PlayingCard width={56} />
              <PlayingCard width={56} />
              <PlayingCard width={56} />
            </div>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>4 players:</strong> the full deck, a 4-card crib and 12 cards each.</li>
              <li>
                <strong>5 players:</strong> take out the 2♣, 2♦ and 2♠, leaving 49 cards: a 4-card crib and 9 cards each. The 2♥
                stays in, so there are still 26 penalty points.
              </li>
              <li>Whoever <strong>wins the first trick wins the crib</strong>. Its cards count toward their score.</li>
              <li>Only the crib winner gets to see what was in it. Everyone else finds out at the end of the hand.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">
            Since the crib might hide the Queen, the Jack, or a handful of hearts, the first trick is a gamble every time.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="passing" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Passing</h2>
          <p>After the deal, everyone chooses <strong>3 cards</strong> to pass. The direction rotates every hand:</p>
          <div class="cycle">
            <div><span>1</span>Left</div>
            <div><span>2</span>Right</div>
            <div><span>3</span>Across</div>
            <div><span>4</span>Keep</div>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">
            With five players there are two “across” seats, so the rotation is left, right, <strong>left across</strong> (two
            seats to your left), <strong>right across</strong> (two seats to your right), then keep. On a keep hand nobody passes. Passed cards arrive marked <span class="new-chip">new</span> so you can spot them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="play" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Playing a hand</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              The player holding the <strong>lowest club</strong> leads it to start the first trick: normally the 2♣, or the 3♣
              with five players. If that card is hiding in the crib, the next-lowest club leads instead.
            </li>
            <li>
              Play goes clockwise (to the left). You must <strong>follow suit</strong> if you can. If you can’t, play anything.
            </li>
            <li>The highest card of the suit that was led wins the trick. The winner leads the next one.</li>
            <li>
              On the first trick nobody may throw hearts or the Queen of Spades, unless that’s all they have. (The host can turn
              this off.)
            </li>
            <li>
              You can’t <strong>lead hearts</strong> until hearts are “broken”, meaning someone has thrown a heart on an earlier
              trick, unless you have nothing but hearts.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="scoring" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Scoring</h2>
          <p>At the end of each hand, count up the cards you took in tricks (and the crib, if you won it):</p>
          <div class="score-cards">
            <div class="score-card">
              <div class="cards"><PlayingCard card="2H" width={64} /><PlayingCard card="KH" width={64} /></div>
              <strong>+1</strong><span class="muted">each heart</span>
            </div>
            <div class="score-card">
              <div class="cards"><PlayingCard card="QS" width={64} /></div>
              <strong>+13</strong><span class="muted">Queen of Spades</span>
            </div>
            <div class="score-card good">
              <div class="cards"><PlayingCard card="JD" width={64} /></div>
              <strong>−10</strong><span class="muted">Jack of Diamonds</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">
            There are 26 penalty points in every hand. Everything else (clubs, the other diamonds and spades) is worth nothing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="shooting" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Shooting the Moon & Sun</h2>
          <div class="shoot">
            <div class="shoot-card moon">
              <span class="icon">☾</span>
              <h3>Shooting the Moon</h3>
              <p>
                Take <strong>all 13 hearts and the Queen of Spades</strong>, crib included. You score 0 for them and everyone
                else takes <strong>+26</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="shoot-card sun">
              <span class="icon">☀</span>
              <h3>Shooting the Sun</h3>
              <p>
                Win <strong>every single trick</strong> of the hand. You score 0 and everyone else takes <strong>+52</strong>. The
                Sun replaces the Moon, so it isn’t counted twice.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="muted">
            The Jack of Diamonds still counts for whoever took it, so a Sun shooter (who takes every card) walks away with −10.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="ending" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Ending the game</h2>
          <p>
            The game always ends on a <strong>finished hand</strong>, never partway through one. Lowest total wins.
          </p>
          <ul class="tips">
            <li>
              By default there’s <strong>no score limit</strong>. Scores keep climbing for as long as the family keeps playing.
              When the season’s over, the host marks the current hand as the final one, and the game ends once it’s scored.
            </li>
            <li>
              The host can also set a <strong>score limit</strong> at any time. Crossing it mid-hand doesn’t end anything. The game
              ends after the first completed hand in which someone is at or over the limit.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="online" class="panel panel-pad">
          <h2>Playing online</h2>
          <ul class="tips">
            <li><strong>Take your time.</strong> Every move is saved instantly. Close the tab and come back tomorrow, and your seat is waiting.</li>
            <li><strong>It updates live.</strong> When others are at the table, you’ll see their cards land as they play.</li>
            <li><strong>Turn alerts.</strong> Switch on “Alert me when it’s my turn” at the table to get a notification while the tab is open.</li>
            <li><strong>Short a player?</strong> The host can fill empty seats with computer players before starting.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Want to practice?</strong> A <a href="/playtest">playtest table</a> is a solo sandbox. You can see every
              hand, drive the computer players and stack the deck, and it doesn’t count toward your stats.
            </li>
            <li><strong>On a phone?</strong> Tap a card to lift it, then tap again (or press Play) to play it.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 17px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: 84px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .toc a {
    padding: 6px 14px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-left: -1px;
    border-left: 1px solid transparent;
  }

  .toc a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
    border-left-color: var(--heart);
  }

  .doc section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 560;
    font-size: 24px;
  }

  .doc p,
  .doc li {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .callout {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 18px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .callout ul,
  .tips {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .crib-demo {
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
  }

  .crib-demo > :global(*:not(:first-child)) {
    margin-left: -38px;
  }

  .cycle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .cycle div {
    padding: 12px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.03);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .cycle span {
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    background: var(--heart-soft);
    color: var(--heart);
  }

  .new-chip {
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 99px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--mint);
    color: #04261a;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .steps {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .score-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .score-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 18px 12px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .score-card .cards {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .score-card strong {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #ff98a4;
  }

  .score-card.good strong {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .shoot {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .shoot-card {
    padding: 18px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .shoot-card h3 {
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .shoot-card p {
    font-size: 14.5px !important;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .shoot-card .icon {
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .moon {
    background: linear-gradient(140deg, rgb(124 180 255 / 0.14), rgb(139 99 210 / 0.08));
    border: 1px solid rgb(124 180 255 / 0.25);
  }

  .moon .icon {
    color: var(--sky);
  }

  .sun {
    background: linear-gradient(140deg, rgb(242 196 109 / 0.16), rgb(240 71 91 / 0.08));
    border: 1px solid rgb(242 196 109 / 0.3);
  }

  .sun .icon {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .toc {
      display: none;
    }

    .callout {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .cycle {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }

    .score-cards,
    .shoot {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
